F01 | H:Performance aggregate renders only the seven comparable whitelist fields, each with definition, included channels/accounts, period, freshness, and coverage | E:zero eligible coverage renders named coverage/N/A rather than a fabricated aggregate | F:native-only or unsupported metric is neither summed nor rendered as a comparable total | source exact phrase: Home aggregates only the approved comparable whitelist, with definition and time range.
F02 | H:provider/account/post native row retains original metric name, unit, definition, source, and collected_at | E:two providers with same-named but differently unitized metrics remain separate rows | F:no cross-provider sum or normalization of native engagement occurs | source exact phrase: Native provider metrics remain separate and retain native names/units.
F03 | H:actual provider-returned zero is rendered as numeric 0 with collected provenance | E:no-data/partial, permission-denied, delayed/stale, error, and unsupported each render their distinct state, reason, denominator treatment, and repair where available | F:a missing/non-collected metric never renders as 0 or enters the aggregate denominator | source exact phrase: Zero, not-collected, permission-denied, delayed, stale, and unsupported are distinct.
F04 | H:analytics row binds displayed value to exact account, artifact revision, publication, and period | E:changing account, filter, or time range atomically refreshes both value and all displayed context | F:prior account/revision/publication/period context is never retained beside a new value | source exact phrase: Analytics states the exact account, content revision, publication, and period measured.
F05 | H:eligible insight shows observation, sample/window, evidence links, confidence, limitation, and alternative explanation as a hypothesis | E:small or biased sample produces hold/exploratory state with the unmet gate named | F:no insight states causal certainty or unsupported causation | source exact phrase: Learning is an evidence-qualified hypothesis, not a causal claim from thin data.
F06 | H:owner-approved next action records exactly one changed variable, before/after rule, approver, effective revision, and result IDs in generation input | E:unapproved or multi-variable proposal remains non-applied/hold | F:objective, audience, offer, CTA, knowledge, guide, account, format, media, and schedule do not change with the approved variable | source exact phrase: Customer can approve one changed variable for the next generation.
F07 | H:new artifact visibly identifies the applied result, shows revision diff, and binds performance evidence | E:undo creates a baseline-derived revision and hold leaves the earlier artifact unchanged | F:an artifact cannot claim performance application when unapproved variables changed or evidence is absent | source exact phrase: The next artifact visibly proves performance feedback was applied.
F08 | H:alert distinguishes observe, draft, approve, and execute; a named human approval audits the exact permitted action before execution | E:rejected or expired approval preserves recommendation/draft and keeps external state unchanged | F:reply, delete, repost, or spend is never automatic or executable merely from an alert | source exact phrase: Alerts and next actions remain safe recommendations until a human approves the exact action.
G01 | H:customer Settings displays all eight customer-owned groups with permitted owner action and named state | E:member/non-owner attempted write is denied while permitted read remains scoped | F:operator field or raw secret appears in no customer DOM, network, log, or export surface | source exact phrase: Customer Settings contains the eight customer-owned groups and no operator secrets.
G02 | H:only a DB-source operator OAuth app Client Secret is revealed once after fresh exact operator reauth plus explicit intent/reason, no-store response, audit actor/reason/time, and manual/30-second DOM clear | E:env source imports atomically to encrypted DB before a fresh reauth can reveal it; concurrent import preserves an existing DB set | F:public, customer, wrong-operator, cross-tenant, absent/expired-reauth, or env-direct HTTP reveal returns raw0 | source exact phrase: Operator OAuth app Client Secret is the one deliberate timed-reveal exception, never a universal “raw secret readback” ban or an unrestricted reveal.
G03 | H:owner-approved, time-bounded operator support can inspect/manage tenant status and recovery with actor, tenant, reason, and time audit | E:cancelled, expired, or unapproved support request leaves prior tenant state intact with no support access | F:operator cannot publish, schedule, approve, reject, delete, mutate/reveal credential, or mutate role as customer | source exact phrase: Admin can manage tenant status/support recovery but cannot publish as the customer by default.
G04 | H:each route25/destination26 entry retains its route, owner, customer purpose, and distinct primary action | E:route manifest diff identifies a changed owner/purpose/action as a review failure | F:no route/destination is silently removed, bounced, or replaced by a generic-template surface | source exact phrase: Route ownership preserves all route25/destination26 surfaces without flattening their different jobs.
G05 | H:customer-facing Korean copy gives state, reason, and next action; technical diagnostics only appear in a contextual support view | E:recoverable error exposes a safe correlation/action without stack detail | F:DOM scan finds no FR/AC/TC/L IDs, localhost, mock/prototype, internal route, provider-internal jargon, or stack text | source exact phrase: Customer copy uses product language, not PRD IDs, code paths, mock/prototype claims, or internal provider jargon.
G06 | H:at 1440, 1024, and 390 each critical action is readable, focusable, and operable | E:mobile drawer/sticky controls preserve bottom padding and keyboard path while content scrolls | F:overflow, hidden navigation, element overlap, or actionable-content occlusion—including Studio bulk bar over review/Save/approve/publish/schedule—is absent | source exact phrase: 1440, 1024, and 390 layouts keep every critical action readable and operable.
G07 | H:entry, Studio, Inbox, Calendar, account, Settings, and Admin expose semantic labels, visible focus, AA contrast, 44px targets, keyboard-safe dialog/drawer, and reduced motion | E:invalid input announces an associated live error and dialog focus returns safely on close | F:no error is unassociated/silent and no keyboard user is trapped or loses the required control | source exact phrase: Focus, labels, contrast, error association, and reduced-motion behavior are accessible.
G08 | H:evidence record separately labels prototype-observed, code-tested, sandbox-tested, and production-observed; semantic E2E follows one campaign/account/revision and provider adapter call plus readback | E:unobserved provider behavior remains explicitly unobserved rather than promoted to production evidence | F:route click/static fixture alone cannot pass real external/provider behavior | source exact phrase: Design acceptance proves customer semantics, while build acceptance separately proves real external behavior.
G09 | H:default screens show class-specific metadata only—OAuth identity/scopes/expiry/health/readiness; tenant token label/created/last-used/revoked; operator source/health/mask; BYOK configured/billing owner/health—and each class has rotate/revoke/health evidence | E:tenant token plaintext appears exactly once on issue then hash/list/reveal0; DB-source operator reveal follows G02; env HTTP reveal0/import-first | F:customer OAuth and BYOK raw0, and every class leaks raw/prefix through no DOM/network/log/error/analytics/export/cross-role/cross-tenant path | source exact phrase: Secret handling is classified by credential purpose: channel OAuth raw0, tenant automation token plaintext1 at issue, operator OAuth app timed reveal under strict control, and BYOK write-only/masked.
H01 | H:at 390, 1024, and 1440 the publish/approve decision surface visibly shows identity, readiness, target, approval consequence, rights, and exact blocker/repair | E:unready account or missing rights remains visible with named recovery without opening hidden help | F:progressive disclosure never hides consequential identity/readiness/approval/rights/publish information | source exact phrase: Progressive disclosure must not hide account identity, readiness, approval, rights, or publish consequences.
H02 | H:only persisted server-read verified state advances exactly one named onboarding/readiness step | E:partial/fault state names its remaining condition and reload/API failure/stale cache does not celebrate | F:route visit, callback without identified/scoped persisted account, or local draft adds zero completion | source exact phrase: Endowed progress must never mark setup steps complete from mere route visit, callback, or local draft.
H03 | H:fresh tenant defaults external publish and community messaging OFF; explicit opt-in names account/scope and approval consequence, is reversible, and is audited | E:cancelled or failed opt-in leaves setting OFF and records no external call | F:before opt-in, publish/message external call count is zero | source exact phrase: Defaults may bias users, so external publish and community messaging default OFF with explicit account and approval consequence.
H04 | H:novice reaches a valid first draft through contextual Text→Photo/Card→Video and Social→Messaging categories; expert can direct-jump/search/recent/template | E:unavailable capability is disabled with a truthful reason and recovery action | F:no valid platform/tool is deleted solely under a “fewer options is always better” psychology claim | source exact phrase: Do not claim “fewer options is always better”; choice-overload effects are heterogeneous and context-dependent.
